  "notes": "The research describes one artist with two documented kits twelve years apart — a D.I.T.C.-lineage swung kit through the 90s, and from 2001 a four-on-the-floor-adjacent club kick with a clap backbeat. Averaging those produces a beat that is neither, so the split is authored as `modes` (`d.i.t.c.` and `terror squad club`) and the top-level block sits between them. Because arrays replace rather than append, this also drops the boom-bap parent's dusty/jazzy/hard moods, which is correct: the two eras are the two records this name actually makes. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it medium-high; the specifically inferred parameter is `bassline.glideProb` — the research says \"synth sub with short glides on the crossover records\" but gives no rate, and 0.2 is a guess sized so a glide reads as an occasional gesture rather than a portamento style. ⚠ `snare.layerClapOffsetMs` carries the club-era clap backbeat; the 90s half is the rimshot-free straight snare the D.I.T.C. entry describes, which is why `rimshotLayer` is false at the top level. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 46 to 45 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 46 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 1.",
